description:
Since the cut-over (#2758, 2026-10-09 00:16 UTC) the oracle is the required soundness reviewer, but every review it posts opens with `### oracle-review-shadow: <state> for <sha>`, its commit status context is `oracle-review-shadow` (`status_context` in .github/oracle-reviewers.yml), and its workflow is .github/workflows/oracle-review-shadow.yml with a matching run name. Readers take "shadow" to mean the result is advisory. The name was kept on purpose through the cut-over because the required checker (_project/scripts/oracle_review_check.py `_ORACLE_VERDICT`) and the soundness merge digest parse the first line byte for byte.

Rename in one coordinated change:
- the posted first line (report.py) and the status context;
- the required checker accepts both the old and the new first line, at least while any open pull request's latest oracle review uses the old one;
- the soundness merge digest accepts the old first line permanently, because it reads merged history;
- the workflow file, its run name, and every `gh workflow run oracle-review-shadow.yml` command in docs, Makefile and handoff text;
- tests and the pr2769 history fixture.

The new status context must not be `oracle-review`: that is the required check's name, so a commit status of that name posted by the App could satisfy the required context without the checker running. Something like `oracle-verdict` avoids the clash. Check the ruleset's required-context source binding before choosing.
